IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part VIII.6 (Temporary Measures), Weekly insurable earnings (s 153.197).
-- Written by piece ei6 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30; nothing here is
-- claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Seat: a person whose benefit period begins from September 26 to November 20, 2021 and asks what weekly insurable
-- earnings are used to work out their rate of benefits.
--
-- Part VIII.6 has no cessation section: its own period ends the provision. A rule here returns a MAYBE, and NOTHING
-- means that the section does not apply to this claimant, so section 14, section 152.16 or paragraph 8.1(a) of the Fishing
-- Regulations (outside this piece) decide.

§ `Section 153.197 - weekly insurable earnings`

-- src:3088 | 153.197 (1) Despite subsection 14(2), the weekly insurable earnings of a claimant whose benefit period begins during the period beginning on September 26, 2021 and ending on November 20, 2021 are deemed to be the greater of
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.197(1) (src:3088)
GIVETH A `Period of days`
`s 153.197 the period in which a benefit period must begin` MEANS
    `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2021 9 26), (YearMonthDay 2021 11 20)

-- src:3090 | (b) $545.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.197(1) (src:3090)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 153.197 the floor of the weekly insurable earnings` MEANS 545

-- (1): despite subsection 14(2), the weekly insurable earnings of a claimant whose benefit period begins from September 26,
-- 2021 to November 20, 2021 are deemed to be the greater of (a) the insurable earnings in the calculation period of
-- subsection 14(4) divided by the number of weeks in that period in which they had insurable earnings, and (b) $545.
-- With no week of insurable earnings (a) cannot be worked out and the text does not say what then: NOTHING (fork F-ei6-13).
-- src:3088 | 153.197 (1) Despite subsection 14(2), the weekly insurable earnings of a claimant whose benefit period begins during the period beginning on September 26, 2021 and ending on November 20, 2021 are deemed to be the greater of
-- src:3089 | (a) the claimant’s insurable earnings in the calculation period referred to in subsection 14(4), divided by the number of weeks in that period in which they had insurable earnings, and
-- src:3090 | (b) $545.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.197(1) (src:3088-3090)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the insurable earnings in the calculation period referred to in subsection 14(4)` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: section 14(4) (piece ei1)
      `the number of weeks in that period in which the claimant had insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: section 14(4) (piece ei1)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.197(1) the weekly insurable earnings of the claimant are deemed to be` IS
    IF     `the day` `the first day of the benefit period` `falls within` `s 153.197 the period in which a benefit period must begin`
       AND `the number of weeks in that period in which the claimant had insurable earnings` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST (IF `the insurable earnings in the calculation period referred to in subsection 14(4)` DIVIDED BY `the number of weeks in that period in which the claimant had insurable earnings` GREATER THAN `s 153.197 the floor of the weekly insurable earnings`
               THEN `the insurable earnings in the calculation period referred to in subsection 14(4)` DIVIDED BY `the number of weeks in that period in which the claimant had insurable earnings`
               ELSE `s 153.197 the floor of the weekly insurable earnings`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (2): a self-employed person whose benefit period begins in that period: a result of dividing the aggregate of the
-- amounts in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b) by 52 that is less than $545 is deemed to be $545.
-- src:3092 | (2) Despite subsection 152.16(1), if a self-employed person’s benefit period begins during the period beginning on September 26, 2021 and ending on November 20, 2021 and the result obtained by dividing the aggregate of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b) by 52 is less than $545, the result is deemed to be $545.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.197(2) (src:3092)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the aggregate of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b)` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: section 152.16 (piece ei5)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.197(2) the result of dividing the aggregate by 52, for a self-employed person` IS
    IF `the day` `the first day of the benefit period` `falls within` `s 153.197 the period in which a benefit period must begin`
    THEN JUST (IF `the aggregate of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b)` DIVIDED BY 52 LESS THAN `s 153.197 the floor of the weekly insurable earnings`
               THEN `s 153.197 the floor of the weekly insurable earnings`
               ELSE `the aggregate of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b)` DIVIDED BY 52)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3): a fisher whose benefit period begins in that period: despite paragraph 8.1(a) of the Employment Insurance
-- (Fishing) Regulations (not among the inputs), the greater of the amount determined under that paragraph and $545.
-- src:3094 | (3) Despite paragraph 8.1(a) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations, the weekly insurable earnings of a fisher whose benefit period begins during the period beginning on September 26, 2021 and ending on November 20, 2021 are deemed to be the greater of the amount determined under that paragraph and $545.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.197(3) (src:3094)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the weekly insurable earnings determined under paragraph 8.1(a) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.197(3) the weekly insurable earnings of the fisher are deemed to be` IS
    IF `the day` `the first day of the benefit period` `falls within` `s 153.197 the period in which a benefit period must begin`
    THEN JUST (IF `the weekly insurable earnings determined under paragraph 8.1(a) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations` GREATER THAN `s 153.197 the floor of the weekly insurable earnings`
               THEN `the weekly insurable earnings determined under paragraph 8.1(a) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations`
               ELSE `s 153.197 the floor of the weekly insurable earnings`)
    ELSE NOTHING
